      {
        "id": 108,
        "name": "Google Shape;108;p2",
        "text": "Understanding the Problem",
        "left": 2893218,
        "top": 381000,
        "width": 6381750,
        "height": 954107
      },
      {
        "id": 110,
        "name": "Google Shape;110;p2",
        "text": "An automation process that reduces the noise generated by the various vulnerability alerts from the scanning tools into a concise list of actual vulnerabilities that a human can validate in a short time period. ",
        "left": 615225,
        "top": 1566200,
        "width": 9497100,
        "height": 1200600
      },
      {
        "id": 112,
        "name": "Google Shape;112;p2",
        "text": "Firms deploy various security scanners (such as Trivy, Semgrep, Nuclei, and Nessus). Each scanner provides their results in a different way, with differing severity levels, repeated detection of the same underlying vulnerabilities without evidence of exploitability. Security professionals have to manually cross-reference findings from different scanners and decide on priorities for themselves. ",
        "left": 615225,
        "top": 3272000,
        "width": 5480700,
        "height": 2862900
      },
      {
        "id": 114,
        "name": "Google Shape;114;p2",
        "text": "● Security analysts (SOC, vulnerability management teams) \n● DevSecOps engineers\n● MSSPs managing multiple clients \n● Organisations with limited security resources \n​",
        "left": 6215064,
        "top": 4012406,
        "width": 4988700,
        "height": 2524200
      },
      {
        "id": 115,
        "name": "Google Shape;115;p2",
